\begin{align}
\ce{NaH2PO4 + 2H2O \rightarrow 2NaH2PO4^{\cdot} + H2O}
\end{align}

The chemical reaction that causes the electrical charge to form in baking soda is:

\begin{align}
\ce{NaH2PO4^{\cdot} + 2H2O \rightarrow Na2HPO4 + H2O + H3O+}
\end{align}

Baking powder and baking soda are both used to leaven bread and other baked goods.  Baking powder is usually more widely used, but baking soda is sometimes used in recipes that call for baking powder.

